L["WELCOME_TEXT"] = "Welcome to Tessera!\n\nYour information blocks are at the top of the screen. Would you like a quick look at how it works?"
L["WELCOME_HELP"] = "Show help"
L["WELCOME_LATER"] = "Later"
L["HELP_TEXT"] = "|cffffd100In short|r\n- Click \"Unlock blocks\", drag the blocks where you like, drop them against each other to merge them, then click \"Lock\".\n- Hover a block for its details, click it to open the matching window, right-click it for its settings.\n- Each block is set up in the Blocks tab; the look of all blocks in the General tab (Style).\n- A block lost off screen: General tab, \"Bring blocks back on screen\". A problem: /tessera bug.\n\nPick a topic on the left for the details.\n\n|cffffd100Placing blocks|r\n1. Click \"Unlock blocks\": the blocks turn blue and the placement banner appears.\n2. Drag a block (or its whole group). Golden lines show alignments; blocks snap to each other, to the grid and to some Blizzard frames.\n3. Drop it against another block (left, right, above or below): they merge.\n4. Click \"Lock\" on the banner.\n\n- Shift + drag: take a block out of its group.\n- Ctrl + click: hide a block (show it again in the Blocks tab).\n- Ctrl + Z, or Undo on the banner: undo the last action.\n- Alt + right-click: quick menu (hide, detach, freeze the group...).\n- The banner can be dragged anywhere and remembers its place; it steps aside while the options window is open.\n- Blizzard's Edit Mode can unlock the blocks too (option in the General tab).\n\n|cffffd100Using blocks|r\n- Hover: details in the tooltip; the blue lines say what each click does.\n- Left click: opens the matching window (bags, character, map, professions, Legacy...). Mouse wheel on the volume block: volume.\n- Shift + click: copies the value into the chat. Middle click: your choice (Behaviour tab).\n- Right click: settings of the block. Alt + right-click: quick menu.\n- Launcher and DataBroker blocks pass every click on to their addon; Alt + right-click still opens Tessera's quick menu.\n\nMail, whispers, reputation, currencies, reagents, ammo and instances only appear when they have something to show, in a second row under the main bar. Friends, guild, talents, group... do the same (\"Hide when empty\" in the Behaviour tab).\n\n|cffffd100Blocks tab|r\nPick \"All blocks\" (or \"All launchers\") to change every block at once, or a single block.\n- Display: what is shown, progress bar, opacity, layer, width (or \"Fit width to text\"), height, scale of its group.\n- Text: font, size, outline, alignment, color.\n- Frame: background, border, and the icon (size, square or round frame, black and white).\n- Behaviour: the block's own settings (gold format, clock, goal, thresholds...), hiding (combat, instances, vehicle or flight, resting), \"Show only on hover\", Shift + click and middle click, alerts, tooltip position.\n- At the bottom: Reset, Copy style to all, Remove (launcher, DataBroker or spacer). \"Add a spacer\" creates an empty block, a separator line or a text title.\n\n|cffffd100General tab|r\n- Style of the blocks and of this window: FlareUI 2.x and 1.x, ElvUI, EllesmereUI, Blizzard, Clean, Transparent. When an interface with a matching style is installed, a window offers it; Tessera never changes your style on its own.\n- Scale of all blocks, lock, snapping, merging, grid, \"Unlock with Edit Mode\", \"Bring blocks back on screen\".\n- Combat, click help in tooltips, quiet chat, minimap button, accessibility (colorblind colors, high contrast, minimum text size).\n\n|cffffd100Launchers and DataBroker|r\n- Launchers tab: turns a minimap or addon compartment button into a block.\n- DataBroker blocks (same tab): another addon's DataBroker object (a value or a button) as a block; type in the search box to find one. A block whose addon is disabled keeps its settings and hides.\n- Broker tab: shares Tessera's blocks with Titan Panel, ChocolateBar, Bazooka... When such an addon is installed, Tessera switches to DataBroker mode and shows no block of its own (a window explains it the first time). A button (or /tessera broker) leaves that mode; the choice only applies to that display addon. \"Back to the automatic choice\" forgets your choices. Blocks that open a Blizzard window cannot do it from another addon's bar.\n\n|cffffd100WoW Forever|r\n- Legacy points block: your points on the Legacy track; the next reward and every reward in its tooltip; a click opens the Legacy panel.\n- Weapon skills block: read from Forever's skill list; the tooltip lists every skill.\n- Professions, talents and Legacy blocks open Forever's own windows.\n\n|cffffd100Profiles|r\nOne profile for all characters or one per character; new, duplicate, delete, reset; export and import as text (to share a layout); a profile used automatically in dungeons and raids; ready-made layouts (top bar, bottom bar, left column, compact).\n\n|cffffd100About and translations|r\n- About tab: version, author, translators, license, source code, and the Changelog (what changed in each version). After an update, a window offers to open it.\n- Tessera is in English and French. Other languages are translated by players with CurseForge's localization tool (Localization page of the Tessera project): your help is welcome!\n\n|cffffd100Commands|r\n/tessera or /tes: options\n/tessera lock, /tessera unlock: lock or unlock the blocks\n/tessera reset: back to the default layout\n/tessera recover: bring back blocks that stick out of the screen\n/tessera minimap: show or hide the minimap button\n/tessera preview: sample values in every block (for screenshots)\n/tessera broker: DataBroker mode on or off\n/tessera bug: report to copy into a bug report\n\nKey bindings (game's key bindings, AddOns category, Tessera): show / hide all blocks (in combat, hiding waits for the end of the fight), lock / unlock, options."
